  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Turn Sequence**: Players take turns in clockwise order, starting with the player to the dealer's left. 2. **Draw Phase**: On your turn, you must draw either the top card of the face-down stock OR the top card of the discard pile. 3. **Replacement Phase**: You must use the drawn card to replace exactly one card in your 3Ã—3 grid (if you drew from the discard pile, you cannot simply discard it again). Replace either a face-down card (revealing it) or a face-up card (which goes to the discard pile). 4. **Revealing**: If you replace a face-down card, it is now revealed to all players. 5. **End of Round**: The round ends immediately when one player has all nine cards face-up. That player does NOT take the remaining turns in that round.",
    Player: "1. **Turn Sequence**: Players take turns in clockwise order, starting with the player to the dealer's left. 2. **Draw Phase**: On your turn, you must draw either the top card of the face-down stock OR the top card of the discard pile. 3. **Replacement Phase**: You must use the drawn card to replace exactly one card in your 3Ã—3 grid (if you drew from the discard pile, you cannot simply discard it again). Replace either a face-down card (revealing it) or a face-up card (which goes to the discard pile). 4. **Revealing**: If you replace a face-down card, it is now revealed to all players. 5. **End of Round**: The round ends immediately when one player has all nine cards face-up. That player does NOT take the remaining turns in that round.",
    objective: 'Win the round by achieving the lowest total score when all nine cards in your grid are face-up.',
    gameplay: "1. **Turn Sequence**: Players take turns in clockwise order, starting with the player to the dealer's left. 2. **Draw Phase**: On your turn, you must draw either the top card of the face-down stock OR the top card of the discard pile. 3. **Replacement Phase**: You must use the drawn card to replace exactly one card in your 3Ã—3 grid (if you drew from the discard pile, you cannot simply discard it again). Replace either a face-down card (revealing it) or a face-up card (which goes to the discard pile). 4. **Revealing**: If you replace a face-down card, it is now revealed to all players. 5. **End of Round**: The round ends immediately when one player has all nine cards face-up. That player does NOT take the remaining turns in that round.",
    keyRules: [
      'Grid Layout: Maintain a strict 3Ã—3 arrangement; cards cannot be rearranged after initial placement.',
      'Face-Up Requirement: You must turn face-down cards face-up by replacing them.',
      'Column Matching Bonus: Three cards of identical rank in the same vertical column score zero points (not horizontal or diagonal).',
      'Discard Rule: If you take the top discard, you MUST use it to replace a card in your grid (cannot simply discard it).',
      'No Card Rearrangement: Once cards are placed, you cannot move themâ€”only replace them.',
      'End Condition: The round ends as soon as any player turns their final face-down card face-up.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 8 players (optimal with 3-5).',
      deck: 'One or two standard 52-card decks (one deck sufficient for 2-4 players; two decks for 5-8 players).',
      equipment: 'Scorepad and pencils for tracking round scores.',
      dealing: 'Dealer distributes nine cards face-down to each player, one at a time, in clockwise order. Each player arranges their cards in a 3Ã—3 grid (three rows of three cards). Before play begins, each player selects three of their nine cards to turn face-up; the remaining six stay face-down. The remaining deck is placed in the center as the stock, and the top card is flipped face-up beside it to start the discard pile.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Turn Sequence**: Players take turns in clockwise order, starting with the player to the dealer's left. 2. **Draw Phase**: On your turn, you must draw either the top card of the face-down stock OR the top card of the discard pile. 3. **Replacement Phase**: You must use the drawn card to replace exactly one card in your 3Ã—3 grid (if you drew from the discard pile, you cannot simply discard it again). Replace either a face-down card (revealing it) or a face-up card (which goes to the discard pile). 4. **Revealing**: If you replace a face-down card, it is now revealed to all players. 5. **End of Round**: The round ends immediately when one player has all nine cards face-up. That player does NOT take the remaining turns in that round.",
