      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Turn Sequence**: Players take turns in clockwise order, starting with the player to the dealer's left. 2. **Draw Phase**: On your turn, you must draw either the top card of the face-down stock OR the top card of the discard pile. 3. **Replacement Phase**: You must use the drawn card to replace exactly one card in your 3Ã—3 grid (if you drew from the discard pile, you cannot simply discard it again). Replace either a face-down card (revealing it) or a face-up card (which goes to the discard pile). 4. **Revealing**: If you replace a face-down card, it is now revealed to all players. 5. **End of Round**: The round ends immediately when one player has all nine cards face-up. That player does NOT take the remaining turns in that round.",
